# #5833, revision 2's erratum. The read-only cold load loads the initiator's floor
# itself rather than the floor plus one. Admission is a stamp at or above the loaded
# value, so a purged incarnation's straddler stamped exactly at the floor is admitted
# above L's recorded close; the claim it replaced refused at the floor.
MODULE: StraddlerBelowInitColdLoadAdmitsAtFloor
TARGET: StraddlerBelowInit
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the cold load loads the floor itself, not the floor plus one
PERTURBS: ColdLoadApply

--- FIND
    /\ loaded' = [loaded EXCEPT ![i] = Max2(@, Max2(rd[i], walFloor[i] + 1))]
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the floor, not the floor plus one.
    /\ loaded' = [loaded EXCEPT ![i] = Max2(@, Max2(rd[i], walFloor[i]))]
--- END
